<h3>2. Migration Steps (Two Parts)</h3>
<p><b>Part A — Key rotation:</b> the migration assistant generates your v2 keys. To carry over
permissions and rate limits without re-entering them, provide your <b>current v1 key + secret</b>
on the migration page — the assistant derives the v2 pair and transfers the permission set.</p>
<p><b>Part B — Address book re-verification:</b> withdrawal whitelisting re-verifies each address
holder. To avoid 17 individual confirmations, the migration page supports <b>batch re-verification</b>:
confirm with your <b>2FA code once</b> (Google Authenticator), and all existing addresses retain
their whitelist status for v2.</p>

