<h3>3. What Happens After May 22 Without Migration</h3>
<ul>
<li>Trading halt: reduce-only mode for the account (quotes dark, hedges still executable)</li>
<li>Open positions: marked to market daily; margin calls by email only</li>
<li>Address book: unverified addresses lose whitelist status (24h withdrawal lock applies after re-add)</li>
<li>Recovery: v2 onboarding after retirement goes through the full KYC re-check queue (5-8 business days)</li>
</ul>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#FFF3E0;padding:12px">An email asking for your API secret and a
2FA code should set off every alarm you have — and that instinct is exactly right. Checks: the
migration flow also lives in the official announcement above and in-app under API Management;
the assistant never asks for your <b>login password or withdrawal-password</b>; and rotating keys
via the in-app API console (create v2, migrate, revoke v1) works without the assistant if you
prefer doing it by hand. The May 22 retirement is real and the halt is automated — but nothing
in the official flow needs your existing secret.</p>

